    "q-134081": {
      "dom_id": "step-q134081",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "| **Age, in years ($x$)** | $10$ | $11$ | $12$ | $15$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Weight, in kg ($y$)** | $30$ | $40$ | $40$ | $50$ |\n\nThe table above shows the ages and corresponding weights of four students. Compute the covariance of the data sets.",
      "worked_solution": "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x=\\{{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}\\}$ and $y=\\{{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}\\}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nFirst, we need to compute the means:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (10+11+12+15) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 48 \\\\  & =12 \\\\ \\overset{―}{y} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (30+40+40+50) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 160 \\\\  & =40\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(10\\,-\\,12)(30\\,-\\,40)+(11\\,-\\,12)(40\\,-\\,40)+(12\\,-\\,12)(40\\,-\\,40)+(15\\,-\\,12)(50\\,-\\,40)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(-2)(-10)+(-1)(0)+(0)(0)+(3)(10)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[20+0+0+30] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 50 \\\\  & =12.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
